      "writtenOn": "2024-06-17T02:54:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi gkolodziejczyk@, seems I missed some context for b/329172203, I wanna double confirm that the final behavior would be:\n\n1. If app attempt to set classic device to active during broadcast, stack will stop broadcast and handover to unicast, audio will be routed to LEA device.\n2. If app stop the broadcast and then set classic device to active, stack will block the handover and audio will be routed to classic device.\n\nIs that correct?",
      "parentUuid": "56031bce_5d745eb1",
      "revId": "3996a0cfc2ab32b4923824f842138ac630c65a5d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f995089_939b7864",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/le_audio/LeAudioService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1927775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-17T11:47:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @yiyishen@google.com\n\nA 1: Broadcast stop is called from upper layers - there is no such logic to stop broadcast and do handover unicast.\nA 2: Yes this is the expected behavior - I thought we agreed on that 😊 there are two steps inside this solution:\n a) Broadcast stop: means that user must agree/application decides to not broadcast audio - why it should broadcast if intention is to switch to classic.\n b) change active/fallback LE Audio device to null - this is basically a normal procedure for changing active device. Changing LE Audio device to null should always result in no fallback device and/or current active device.\n \nFeel free if something is not clear ;)\n\nRegards,\nGrzegorz",
      "parentUuid": "1ad1a470_507f3242",
      "revId": "3996a0cfc2ab32b4923824f842138ac630c65a5d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d17c690_dd22a159",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/le_audio/LeAudioService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944471
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-17T13:24:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A1: Then what\u0027s the intended behavior if app set classic device to active during broadcast? \nA2: Yes we agreed on this;) app side will stop the broadcast first then set active to classic.",
      "parentUuid": "6f995089_939b7864",
      "revId": "3996a0cfc2ab32b4923824f842138ac630c65a5d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
